<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#gross-domestic-product">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gross domestic product</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as GDP, GNP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gross domestic product (GDP) is a measure of the total value of goods and services produced within an economy over a given period. Historians use modern estimates of it to compare pre-modern economies. The profiles cite such estimates for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> at its peak and for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, which had one of the world's largest economies by 1900.</p></div>
